' bug-11: a Fixed literal with an extreme scientific exponent (e.g. 1e9999999999)
' drove expand_scientific_notation into a multi-GB digit-string blowup / hang
' before any range check. fixed_raw_from_decimal now rejects extreme exponents in
' O(1), so the literal is cleanly rejected with TYPE_FIXED_LITERAL_OVERFLOW
' instead of hanging.
FUNC main AS Integer
  LET x AS Fixed = 1e9999999999
  RETURN 0
END FUNC
